 python3 (>= 3.11),
Breaks: copypastebin (<< 1.2~)
Replaces: copypastebin (<< 1.2~)
Description: local analysis backend for CopyPasteBin
 CopyPasteBin's short-lived command-line backend detects selected kinds of
 sensitive text and prepares local redaction suggestions. It does not install
 or enable a GNOME extension, start a service, or send data to a cloud service.

Package: gnome-shell-extension-copypastebin
Section: gnome
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 copypastebin-backend (= ${binary:Version}),
 gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
 gir1.2-glib-2.0,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
 gjs,
 gnome-shell (>= 50~),
 gnome-shell (<< 51~),
Breaks: copypastebin (<< 1.2~)
Replaces: copypastebin (<< 1.2~)
Description: GNOME Shell interface for CopyPasteBin
 CopyPasteBin detects selected kinds of sensitive clipboard text and secrets,
 warns when sensitive content is detected, and helps the user redact text
 before sharing.
 .
 It also provides manual redaction of selected areas in local photos and
 screenshots. Analysis and editing stay on the device; no data is sent to a
 cloud service. This release supports GNOME Shell 50 on Wayland and requires
 explicit per-user activation after installation.

Package: copypastebin
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 copypastebin-backend (= ${binary:Version}),
 gnome-shell-extension-copypastebin (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: complete CopyPasteBin installation for GNOME
 This small package installs the matching CopyPasteBin backend and GNOME Shell
 extension. Keeping the existing package name makes upgrades from the 1.1
 monolithic package install the complete split product.
